From 168a43252287113734131a982227e86056df971d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:45:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] borg: count the newest entry in the recent sale and purchase
 lists

The Borg keeps a short list of what it has just sold (or stored at home)
and just bought, so that it does not immediately buy back what it sold
or sell back what it bought.  The writers stored the index of the entry
they had just written in sold_item_num / bought_item_num, but every
reader scans p < num, so the most recent sale or purchase was never
checked.  After storing three rations at home, a low-level Warrior took
them straight back out on its next store turn.

Keep *_item_num as the number of slots in use: advance the write index
first and raise the count to it.  When the write index wraps, the count
stays at the number of slots the ring uses.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#20.

(cherry picked from commit 9ae5e4585599aa4f3c5dce7c2259fe7e2604cea1)
---
 src/borg/borg-store-buy.c  | 3 ++-
 src/borg/borg-store-sell.c | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c b/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c
index f646863e5..81f22c79f 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c
@@ -1233,8 +1233,9 @@ bool borg_think_shop_buy(void)
         bought_item_tval[bought_item_nxt]  = item->tval;
         bought_item_sval[bought_item_nxt]  = item->sval;
         bought_item_store[bought_item_nxt] = borg.goal.shop;
-        bought_item_num                    = bought_item_nxt;
         bought_item_nxt++;
+        if (bought_item_num < bought_item_nxt)
+            bought_item_num = bought_item_nxt;
 
         /* The purchase is complete */
         borg.goal.shop = borg.goal.ware = borg.goal.item = -1;
diff --git a/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c b/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c
index 906d5826a..bd681e9af 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c
@@ -1131,8 +1131,9 @@ bool borg_think_shop_sell(void)
         sold_item_tval[sold_item_nxt]  = item->tval;
         sold_item_sval[sold_item_nxt]  = item->sval;
         sold_item_store[sold_item_nxt] = borg.goal.shop;
-        sold_item_num                  = sold_item_nxt;
         sold_item_nxt++;
+        if (sold_item_num < sold_item_nxt)
+            sold_item_num = sold_item_nxt;
 
         /* The purchase is complete */
         borg.goal.shop = borg.goal.ware = borg.goal.item = -1;
